# pixi environments
.pixi/*
!.pixi/config.toml
# The MadGraph work area: process directories, the f2py extension modules built
# from their Fortran, and the assembled reference bundle. Generated by the oracle
# layer, fetched by everyone else.
/ee_to_mumu/
/validation/helas/*.so
/validation/madgraph/output
# Fetched LHAPDF6 sets and the compiled oracle generator (its output is committed)
/validation/pdf/NNPDF23_lo_as_0130_qed/
/validation/pdf/NNPDF31_lo_as_0130/
/validation/pdf/*.tar.gz
/validation/pdf/gen_oracle
__pycache__/
# Agent configuration is committed, but under `.agents/` — the cross-tool
# location — with `.claude/` holding symlinks into it. Everything else Claude
# Code writes here (worktree scratch, local settings) is per-machine. A skill or
# agent definition that lands under `.claude/` directly is invisible to
# `git worktree` checkouts and to fresh clones, which is where they get lost.
.claude/*
!.claude/agents
!.claude/skills
.vscode
